      "text": "Let's analyze the given figure step by step to find the longest segment:\n\n1. **Identify the angles and triangles:**\n   - We have an isosceles triangle \\(ABC\\) with angles \\( \\angle BAC = 55^\\circ \\) and \\( \\angle ABC = 40^\\circ \\). Since the sum of internal angles in a triangle is \\(180^\\circ\\), we can calculate \\( \\angle ACB \\) as follows:\n     \\[\n     \\angle ACB = 180^\\circ - \\angle BAC - \\angle ABC = 180^\\circ - 55^\\circ - 40^\\circ = 85^\\circ\n     \\]\n   - This implies that \\( \\angle DAC = 85^\\circ - 55^\\circ = 30^\\circ \\) and \\( \\angle ADB = 85^\\circ - 40^\\circ = 45^\\circ \\).\n\n2. **Analyze the segments \\(AD\\) and \\(BD:**\n   - Observe that \\(AD = AB + BD = 5 + b_1\\) and \\(BD\\) has two valid interpretations based on your diagram.\n   - Easy to see that \\( AD = 5 + b_1 > AB \\).\n\nThus, \\(AD\\) is the longest among the given segments. The answer is \\(\\boxed{AD}\\).",
